  "answer": "- Root cause 1: Partial config PUT overwrote/cleared routing.strategy state, leaving exact remote model resolution without a valid chosen_endpoint_id and producing HTTP 400 with unknown.endpoint / execution_failed.
  - Fix: Restore routing.strategy and use merge-preserving config updates so unspecified fields are not dropped on PUT.
- Root cause 2: Default throughput SLA policy incorrectly hard-denied remote endpoints below 24 TPS even when the exact remote endpoint was the only allow-listed candidate.
  - Fix: Change SLA/eligibility logic so exact/sole allow-listed remote endpoints are not rejected by the default sub-24-TPS gate, or explicitly configure an override/threshold for those endpoints."
}

